ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Contents
==================================================
This page provides help with the most common questions about  [LINK: (Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia] .

Use the search box below, or browse the  [LINK: (Help menu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu]  or the  [LINK: (Help directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Directory]  to search Wikipedia's help pages.

For interactive assistance related to using and editing Wikipedia, see the  [LINK: (help desk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Help_desk]  and the  [LINK: (Teahouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:TH/Q] .


# READ OR FIND AN ARTICLE #

The  [LINK: (Readers' FAQ) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:FAQ/Readers]  and our  [LINK: (about page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:About]  contain the most commonly sought information about Wikipedia.

For simple searches, there is a search bar at the top of every page. Type what you are looking for in the box. Suggested matches will appear in a dropdown list. Select any page in the list to go to that page. Or, select the "Search" button, or press ↵ Enter, to go to a full search result. For advanced searches, see  [LINK: (Help:Searching) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Searching] .

There are other ways to browse and explore Wikipedia articles; many can be found at  [LINK: (Wikipedia:Contents) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Contents] . See our  [LINK: (disclaimer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:General_disclaimer]  for cautions about Wikipedia's limitations.

For  [LINK: (mobile access) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Mobile_access] , press the  [LINK: (mobile view) -> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Contents]  link at the very bottom of every  [LINK: (desktop view) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Contents]  page.


# EDIT AN ARTICLE #

Contributing is easy: see  [LINK: (how to edit a page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Editing] . For a quick summary on participating, see  [LINK: (contributing to Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Contributing_to_Wikipedia] , and for a friendly tutorial, see  [LINK: (our introduction) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction] . For a listing of introductions and tutorials by topic, see  [LINK: (getting started) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Getting_started] . The  [LINK: (Simplified Manual of Style) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:SMOS]  and  [LINK: (Cheatsheet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Cheatsheet]  can remind you of basic  [LINK: (wiki markup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Wikitext] .

[LINK: (Be bold) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Be_bold]  in improving articles! When adding facts, please  [LINK: (provide references) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_referencing/1]  so others may verify them. If you are affiliated with the article subject, please see our  [LINK: (conflict of interest guideline) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Conflict_of_interest] .

The  [LINK: (simple guide to vandalism cleanup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Simple_guide_to_vandalism_cleanup]  can help you undo malicious edits.

If you're looking for places you can help out, the  [LINK: (Task Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Task_Center]  is the place to go, or check out what else is happening at the  [LINK: (community portal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Community_portal] . You can practice editing and experiment in a  [LINK: (sandbox) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Sandbox] your  [LINK: (sandbox) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:MyPage/sandbox] .


# REPORT A PROBLEM WITH AN ARTICLE #

If there is a problem with an article about yourself, a family member, a friend or a colleague, please read  [LINK: (Biographies of living persons/Help) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Biographies_of_living_persons/Help] .

If you spot a problem with an article, you can fix it directly, by clicking on the "Edit" link at the top of that page.  [LINK: (See the "edit an article" section of this page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Contents#edit-heading]  for more information.

If you don't feel ready to fix the article yourself, post a message on the article's  [LINK: (talk page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Talk_page_guidelines] . This will bring the matter to the attention of others who work on that article. There is a "Talk" link at the beginning of every article page.

You can  [LINK: (contact us) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Contact_us_-_Readers] . If it's an article about you or your organization, see  [LINK: (Contact us – Subjects) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Contact_us_-_Subjects] .


# CREATE A NEW ARTICLE OR UPLOAD MEDIA #

Check  [LINK: (Your first article) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Your_first_article]  to see if your topic is appropriate, then the  [LINK: (Article wizard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Article_wizard]  will walk you through creating the article.

Once you have created an article, see  [LINK: (Writing better articles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Writing_better_articles]  for guidance on how to improve it and what to include (like reference  [LINK: (citations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citing_sources] ).

For contributing images, audio or video files, see the  [LINK: (Introduction to uploading images) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_uploading_images/1] . Then the  [LINK: (Upload wizard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:File_Upload_Wizard]  will guide you through that process.


# FAQ AND INTERACTIVE HELP #

Answers to common problems can be found at  [LINK: (frequently asked questions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:FAQ] .

Or check out  [LINK: (where to ask questions or make comments) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Questions] .

New users should seek help at the  [LINK: (Teahouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Teahouse]  if they're having problems while editing Wikipedia.

More complex questions can be posed at the  [LINK: (Help desk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Help_desk] . Volunteers will respond as soon as they're able.

Or  [LINK: (ask for help on your talk page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:MyTalk&action=edit&section=new&preload=Help:Contents/helpmepreload&preloadtitle=Help+me%21]  and a volunteer will visit you there!

You can get live help with editing in the  [LINK: (help chatroom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:IRC_help_disclaimer] .

For help with technical issues, ask at the  [LINK: (Village pump) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Village_pump_(technical)] .


# FACTUAL QUESTIONS #

If  [LINK: (searching Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search]  has not answered your question (for example, questions like "Which country has the world's largest fishing fleet?"), try the  [LINK: (Reference Desk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Reference_desk] . Volunteers there will attempt to answer your questions on any topic, or point you toward the information you need.


# DIRECTORIES #

[LINK: (Directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Directory] : main list of directories and indexes.

[LINK: (Help directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Directory] : for informative, instructional and consultation pages.

[LINK: (Request directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Request_directory] : for services and assistance that can be requested on Wikipedia.

[LINK: (Policy directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:List_of_policies] : official policies for "English Wikipedia".

[LINK: (Guideline directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:List_of_guidelines] : official guidelines for "English Wikipedia".

[LINK: (Manual of Style directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Contents] : pages related to the style manual of Wikipedia articles.

[LINK: (Departments) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Department_directory] : for the different divisions of Wikipedia.

[LINK: (Editor's index) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Editor%27s_index_to_Wikipedia] : for everything an editor needs to know to work on Wikipedia.

[LINK: (Essay directory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Essay_directory] : for Wikipedia namespace essays.

[LINK: (Dashboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Dashboard] : for current discussions taking place throughout Wikipedia.

[LINK: (WikiProjects) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Council/Directory] : for people who want to work together as a team to improve Wikipedia.

[LINK: (Wikitext) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Wikitext] : for the syntax used by Wikipedia to format a page.

[LINK: (HTML) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:HTML_in_wikitext] : for HTML5 elements, or tags and their attribute.

[LINK: (Templates) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Template_index] : for templates used within Wikipedia.


# HELP BY TOPIC #

[LINK: (Help Menu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu] : for searching by subject matter.

[LINK: (Navigating Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Navigating_Wikipedia] : for searching and browsing the encyclopedia.

[LINK: (Joining Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Joining_Wikipedia] : how to get involved.

[LINK: (Editing Wikipedia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Editing_Wikipedia] : has general help for editors.

[LINK: (Links and references) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Links] : has help for creating links, or dealing with references

[LINK: (Images and media) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Images_and_media] : how to use images, videos and sound files.

[LINK: (Keeping track of changes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Tracking_changes] : how to track the evolution of a page, or follow a user.

[LINK: (Policies and guidelines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Policies_and_guidelines] : for community standards.

[LINK: (Asking questions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Asking_questions] : volunteers will attempt to answer.

[LINK: (The Wikipedia community) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/The_Wikipedia_community] : how to submit or debate a proposal.

[LINK: (Resources and lists) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Resources_and_lists] : has resources for editors.

[LINK: (Account settings) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Account_settings_and_maintenance] : has tips and tools for registered users.

[LINK: (Technical information) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Technical_information] : has tools for advanced users, and troubleshooting.

[LINK: (Site map) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Menu/Site_map] : is the above thirteen pages on one single page.


# TIP OF THE DAY #

For contributors, it can be a valuable learning experience to work on  [LINK: (Wikipedia article cleanup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Wikipedia_article_cleanup] . In addition, providing  [LINK: (articles with missing information) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Wikipedia_articles_with_missing_information]  does improve the quality of these existing articles.

There are  [LINK: (articles tagged with content issues) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Wikipedia_articles_with_content_issues]  which 
can be resolved to insure accuracy as the articles are developing. Remember to discuss major additions, changes, and controversial topics on the  [LINK: (article's talk page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Using_talk_pages] .


